OL,3,AMushroom killer must stay in jail
OL,4,Aforever for 'truly dreadful' crime,
OL,5,Aappeal court told
OL,6,
OL,7,FAn Australian court has been told that
OL,8,Fthe crimes of mushroom murderer Erin
OL,9,FPatterson were "truly dreadful" and
OL,10,Fthat she should never be allowed to
OL,11,Fleave prison.
OL,13,FCrown prosecutors are appealing against
OL,14,Fa sentence they call "manifestly
OL,15,Finadequate" as it allows for the
OL,16,Fpossibility of parole.
OL,18,FPatterson was jailed for life after
OL,19,Fkilling three of her relatives and
OL,20,Ftrying to kill another by serving them
OL,21,Fa beef Wellington containing death cap
OL,22,Fmushrooms at her Victoria home in 2023.
OL,23,APub: 20-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
